{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>The fiery serpents.</b> It appears that since Israel spoke against Moses and went further, sinning by speaking against Elohim, HaShem sent upon them that which was born from their sin. For we have already written in other places that from a transgression a harmful force emerges. And through this you will understand the truth of the statement of our Sages of blessed memory (Ta'anit 8a), who said: They asked the serpent: A lion tears and eats, etc. — what pleasure do you have? And he replied: Tell the master of evil speech (ba'al ha-lashon), thus far. The meaning of his answer is that there is a species of transgression from which there emerges a species of harm corresponding to it. And here two things were born from their sin: a serpent (nahash) and a burning one (saraph) — a serpent that has teeth and kills a person, and a burning one that consumes the soul. And HaShem sent them among them, as the verse says: <b>And HaShem sent against the people the fiery serpents.</b> And it says <b>וַיְשַׁלַּח</b> ('and He sent') in the manner of the verse (Job 8:4): ״וַיְשַׁלְּחֵם בְּיַד פִּשְׁעָם״ ('and He sent them through the hand of their transgression'). <b>The serpents</b> correspond to what they spoke against Moses, for anyone who speaks evil speech against his fellow, and all the more so against his teacher, a serpent strikes him. <b>And the fiery ones</b> correspond to what they spoke against Elohim. I further saw in the Midrash (Numbers Rabbah 19:22), and this is its language: ״הַשְּׂרָפִים״ — because they consume (שׂוֹרְפִים) the soul, thus far. And this accords with our words."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:49.552349333Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}